# Intent: Two more games from the owner's list, as data packs (firmware/games/eightball.json, dice.json) on a few engine additions: Magic 8-Ball (shake the unit gently or tap the ball; a dark ball with a floating triangle window, twenty classic answers in English and Spanish, a mysterious hum, a face and a ring light cue) and Dice and Coin (tap to roll one or two big drawn dice or flip a coin, six tumbling frames, a rattle on the roll and a thud or a coin ring on landing, the result big; a gentle shake rolls too). Engine: a die shape and a coin shape (drawn in maipai_games_draw.h), a ring-light action that starts with its sound, four more sound clips (rattle, thud, mystic, ting), 32 texts per pack. Celebrations: a win (Tic-Tac-Toe win, a Rock Paper Scissors round won) and every new best score show confetti (a new best: confetti and fireworks, 4 s) through the overlay engine with the happy face; it sheds under the governor, keeps the banner row and subtitle strip clear and does nothing when overlays are off. Motion: the mole pops with an ease-out overshoot and is squashed when struck, dice hop and bounce, the coin flips, bounces and glints, the eight ball wobbles on a damped spring and its window fades in and floats, the Rock Paper Scissors hands bump with the beat, Tic-Tac-Toe marks draw in, Do It's called tile pulses (arithmetic on existing objects, no new heap). Gentle shake (owner rule: nobody shakes the unit hard): the games get every 20 ms accelerometer sample and use their own detector, where a small quick wobble of a few centimeters counts (strokes of 2.2 m/s^2, three within 0.9 s) and a very violent one (20 m/s^2 or more) does not count and answers "Easy!" with no points; the hints and tiles say "Gentle shake" (Spanish "Agita suave").
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_games.cc, maipai_games_core.h, maipai_games_sfx_core.h, maipai_games_input_core.h, maipai_games_draw.h (ours, G01 to UI14), hal_imu.cpp (M5Stack, one hook), maipai_fx.cc and maipai_fx.h (ours, TA01 to TA04: one exported function), firmware/main/CMakeLists.txt (ours)
